**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The scan as pure Domain data: one or more blocks, each a product of axes read on one capture (001 §K 'a **scan**: one or more variables (dial 0…360 step 20; φ; incidence × azimuth × observable; λ on a tunable source)'; 001 §Q AT-2 'one experiment per plate, with a multi-variable scan (incidence × azimuth × T / R) that reproduces exactly `a1 @ a2 @ a3`': the optic-axis plate joins A1's four azimuths read in T with A2's incidence × azimuth read in T and R, so an experiment holds more than one product; the S9.1 brief: today's `VariableParameter` / `VariableRange` / `sourceWaveLengthOpt` are generalised, not duplicated). Nothing reads it before step 288. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: (1) `VariableRange` (`Experiments.fs:VariableRange`) gains `member this.sweptValues : SweptValue list`: `n = max 2 points` values, the k-th `min + (max − min) · k / (n − 1)` for k = 0 … n − 1, the grid `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun` computes today (`xs`), so a chart built over it keeps every number. (2) After `ElementLabel` (`Experiments.fs:ElementLabel`), in this order: (a) `ScanAxis = { elementId : ElementId; label : ElementLabel; variable : VariableParameter; range : VariableRange }`, one quantity of one slot over its range: step 261's `VariedElement` with its range, which step 288 deletes; `member this.describe : string` is the varied text of `Experiment.description` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`) without its capture, `<label>: vary <variable.label> over <min>…<max> <unit> (<points> pts)`, with the same `%g` and `%d` forms. (b) `ScanSetting = { elementId : ElementId; variable : VariableParameter; value : SweptValue }`, one axis at one value. (c) `ScanPoint = { settings : ScanSetting list; capture : MeasurementMode }`, one configuration: each axis of its block at one value, read on the block's capture. (d) `ScanBlock = { axes : ScanAxis list; capture : MeasurementMode }`, with `member this.points : ScanPoint list`, the product of the axes' `sweptValues` with the first axis outermost and the last innermost, each point carrying the block's capture (so a capture of both branches is the innermost observable, as A2 reads T then R); a block with no axis is one point with no setting, a dark line. (e) `ExperimentScan = { blocks : ScanBlock list; sourceWaveLengthOpt : WaveLength option }`, what an experiment varies, block after block, and the wavelength a tunable source is set to while no axis varies it (spec 0046's `sourceWaveLengthOpt`, now the scan's); `member this.points : ScanPoint list` is the blocks' points in order; `member this.axes : ScanAxis list` the blocks' axes in order; `static member oneAxis (axis : ScanAxis) (capture : MeasurementMode) (sourceWaveLengthOpt : WaveLength option) : ExperimentScan` is one block of that one axis, today's experiment; and `static member darkLine (capture : MeasurementMode) : ExperimentScan` is one block of no axis and no wavelength. No validation, cache, unit conversion or other member is added: a tunable source's limits stay the host's clamp (spec 0046). Tests, in `ExperimentProxyTests`, over test-local element ids `sample` and `analyzer`: `a range sweeps its points evenly from its minimum to its maximum`: `{ min = 0; max = 360; points = 19 }` sweeps 0, 20, …, 360 exactly (dial 0…360 step 20); `{ min = 89; max = 0; points = 3 }` sweeps 89, 44.5 and 0; and a range of one point sweeps its two ends. `a scan block's points are the product of its axes, the first outermost, each read on the block's capture`: the block of `sample`'s R2 over 20…60° (3 points) and `sample`'s R1 over 0…90° (2 points), capture both, has the six points (20, 0), (20, 90), (40, 0), (40, 90), (60, 0), (60, 90) in that order, each with two settings naming `sample` and each `CaptureBoth`; and a block with no axis has one point with no setting. `a scan is its blocks' points in order, so one experiment joins two designs`: the scan of the block `sample`'s R1 over 0…67.5° (4 points) read in T, then the block above, has ten points, the first four `CaptureTransmitted` and the last six `CaptureBoth`, and its `axes` are the three axes in order; `oneAxis` of `analyzer`'s R1 axis read in T at 632.8 nm is one block of that axis keeping the wavelength; and `darkLine CaptureTransmitted` has one point and no wavelength.

**Acceptance.** After the scan shapes land, `VariableRange.sweptValues` MUST be chartForRun's evenly spaced grid, `ScanBlock.points` MUST be the product of its axes with the first outermost and its capture on each point, and `ExperimentScan` MUST join its blocks' points in order and carry the tunable source's setting; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a range sweeps its points evenly from its minimum to its maximum`, `a scan block's points are the product of its axes, the first outermost, each read on the block's capture` and `a scan is its blocks' points in order, so one experiment joins two designs`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.
